      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ravenden Springs was founded in 1883 when businessman R. Welsh built a resort town around the town’s healing springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ravenden_Springs%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s springs were famed for their healing powers, drawing visitors who still come to taste the fresh water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://seerandolphcounty.com/about-randolph-county/ravenden-springs-arkansas/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hall’s Creek Canyon, the town’s most unique feature, offers dramatic cliffs and a historic cave that once housed the first school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://seerandolphcounty.com/2013/06/20/ravenden-springs-arkansas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "At the bluff’s base lies Elephant Cave, named for its enormous size, a popular spot for local explorers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://seerandolphcounty.com/2013/06/20/ravenden-springs-arkansas/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The former Ravenden Springs School, now a museum and community center, sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
